in another battle with Congress a House  committee has voted to hold two members  of the president's cabinet in contempt  over a plan to add a citizenship  question to the 2020 census can you  imagine you send out a census and you're  not allowed to say whether or not a  person's an American citizen the  president is claiming executive  privilege to keep Congress from seeing  documents related to the decision Nancy  Cordes is on Capitol Hill Nancy what  comes next well this is an issue that is  going all the way to the Supreme Court  Michelle later this month the justices  are expected to rule on whether the  citizenship question can be added to the  2020 census White House says they're  just going back to something that has  been asked at various points in the past  but Democrats see politics at work here  and so they have been trying for a year  to try to get their hands on memos and  emails that would show who got the  question added and why but the Justice  and Commerce Department's won't give  them what they want and so the House  Oversight Committee voted yesterday to  hold the leaders of those agencies in  contempt of Congress which could give  the committee's more power to subpoena  these documents Nancy people actually  have a choice whether to answer a  question on the census so why does this  actually matter  well because experts have warned that if  you add a citizenship question it is  going to discourage some number of  immigrant families from answering the  census and so they say that's going to  skew population figures and because  these numbers are used to determine  everything from school funding to  congressional districts Democrats worry  that the immigrant heavy areas that they  often represent are going to end up  suffering as a result they think that's  the real reason this question is being  added Nancy thank you man is he quarters  at the Capitol
 

